Validation and Quality Control
The test method used for the determination of heavy metals meets the criteria of
Regulation (EC) 333/2007 of the Commission of March 28, 2007, which establishes
the sampling and analysis methods for the
control of levels trace elements and process contaminants from food products and
their modifications. The validation was carried out according to the requirements of
the UNE/EN-ISO 17025 Standard for Testing Laboratories, and it is accredited by the
National Accreditation Entity (ENAC). For
MeHg determination, the test method is in
the accreditation process.
